    {
      "text": "There's a worse version of this, and it's about who is allowed to hide. Ask yourself who benefits from privacy and who benefits from transparency, and notice that it's never the same person. The employer wants your salary visible. The bank wants your spending visible. The platform wants your preferences visible. The person with power is usually the one asking for the window. So a rule that makes everyone transparent doesn't make the world equal. It makes the world legible. And legibility has always been more useful to the person looking than to the person being looked at.",
